{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Gutter guards are covers or screens that fit over or inside your gutters. They let water in while blocking leaves, pine needles, twigs, and roof grit. Simple concept — execution is what matters.</p>

<p><strong>Different types for different debris:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Micro-mesh guards use surgical-grade stainless steel mesh. Holes are tiny — about 50 microns. They block pine needles, roof grit, even shingle granules. Best choice if you have significant pine coverage.</li>
<li>Screen guards have larger openings. Good for big leaves, not ideal for needles. More airflow, so they can handle heavier rain flow rates.</li>
<li>Solid covers use surface tension — water sheets around the curve and into the gutter, debris slides off the edge. Work well, but heavy rain can overshoot on steep roofs.</li>
</ul>

<p>The right choice depends on what's actually falling into your gutters, your roof pitch, and how your current system is set up. We assess all of that during the estimate.</p>

<p><strong>What we won't install:</strong> Foam inserts (they decompose and clog within 2 years), cheap plastic screens (they warp in Alabama heat), and any product that requires you to slide it under shingles (that voids roof warranties and causes leaks).</p>
{% endset %}

